# Version pins for the vllmcustom image -- the ONE place they live.
#
# Read by ./container/build (what to build), ./container/push (stale-snapshot
# check) and ./qwen3.8-flash-next/run (which image to run). Plain KEY=value only:
# comments on their own lines, no quotes, no $expansions, no trailing comments,
# so it is valid both for bash `source` and for `docker run --env-file`.
#
# DEFAULT_* names are defaults, not settings: ./container/build reads them as
# ${CUDA_VERSION:-$DEFAULT_CUDA_VERSION} etc., so `CUDA_VERSION=13.0.3
# ./container/build` still overrides without editing this file.
#
# Bumping the main snapshot:
#   1. set VLLM_MAIN_SHA to the new commit, and VLLM_MAIN_FLASHINFER_REF /
#      VLLM_MAIN_TORCH_REF / VLLM_MAIN_TORCHVISION_VERSION to what that commit's
#      requirements/cuda.txt pins (flashinfer-python==X -> vX, torch==Y -> vY,
#      torchvision stays bare). Step 7 of ./repin.md is the full re-check.
#   2. PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1 VLLM_REF=main ./container/build   # seconds; refuses a mismatch
#   3. VLLM_REF=main ./container/build
#      then ./container/push — the owner's step, never the agent's (RULES.md Rule B1 #7)
#      ^ COST: read step 1's torch line before running this. If torch moved, the torch-build
#        layer is dead and the stages are a chain (torch -> torchaudio -> flashinfer -> vllm ->
#        openai), so it is a FULL rebuild measured in HOURS, not the incremental vllm-only
#        rebuild a commit count suggests. ccache barely helps across a torch minor bump.
#        4d9a8d6 is such a bump (torch 2.13 -> 2.14), so the very first run of this new
#        procedure is the expensive one.
#   4. ./qwen3.8-flash-next/run                           # finds the new image by its vllm.ref label
# Nothing else needs editing unless the build or the launcher tells you so.

# 13.2.1. What actually binds the CUDA *minor* here is the torchvision wheel: the
# vllm-openai stage installs it --no-deps from the cu132 index, and both
# torchvision and torchaudio compare their compiled CUDA major.minor against
# torch.version.cuda at import and raise if it differs (transformers imports
# torchaudio at module load, so that raise kills `vllm serve` outright). Index,
# wheel and our source-built torch must all agree on 13.2.
# Do not read torch's own PyPI matrix into this: torch 2.14.0's metadata pulls
# cuda-toolkit==13.0.3.0 and downgrades nvidia-cuda-runtime to 13.0.96. That is
# what PyPI's *prebuilt* wheel targets, and we compile torch from source against
# the system toolkit, so it says nothing about our build. Whether those nvidia-*
# wheels land in the runtime image at all depends on the METADATA OF OUR OWN
# locally-built torch wheel (layer 1 installs /wheels-base/*.whl WITH deps),
# which is unmeasured -- do not assume the shadow exists. What is worth knowing
# is only the diagnostic: if a boot ever dies inside a CUDA/nvrtc call, check
# `importlib.metadata.requires('torch')` in the image before blaming the model.
# 13.3.x is published and the host driver (610.43.03) meets its 610.43.02 floor,
# but no torch/flashinfer/vLLM release has CI on 13.3 yet, and flashinfer notes
# 13.3+ nvcc changed its dry-run output (broke sccache). vLLM itself only
# CI-builds on 13.0.3, so that is the safe fallback variant.
DEFAULT_CUDA_VERSION=13.2.1

# Release set: mutually compatible (vLLM v0.29.0 pins torch 2.13.0 / flashinfer
# 0.6.18 -- see its requirements/cuda.txt; ./container/preflight checks this).
# Not bumped further on purpose (2026-09-11): torch 2.14.0 is out but no vLLM
# *release* pins it, and vLLM's wheel hard-pins flashinfer-python==X, so the
# flashinfer ref can only move together with the vLLM ref.
# The main snapshot no longer agrees with this set: main took torch 2.14.0 in
# vllm#52183, so the DEFAULT_* values below are the RELEASE pins only and the
# snapshot overrides its own (VLLM_MAIN_* further down). Nothing here is a
# default for the snapshot any more except TORCHAUDIO, which has not diverged.
DEFAULT_VLLM_REF=v0.29.0
DEFAULT_TORCH_REF=v2.13.0
DEFAULT_FLASHINFER_REF=v0.6.18
# torchaudio is built from source (pytorch/audio). 2.11.0 is upstream's pairing
# with torch 2.13.0 -- and there is no cu132 torchaudio wheel, while a cu130 one
# refuses to import next to a CUDA 13.2 torch (both torchaudio and torchvision
# compare CUDA major.minor at import). So: source build, against our torch.
DEFAULT_TORCHAUDIO_REF=v2.11.0
# torchvision stays a prebuilt wheel, from the CUDA-minor-matched index.
DEFAULT_TORCHVISION_VERSION=0.28.0

# Main snapshot (VLLM_REF=main ./container/build): the commit pinned here, NOT
# the moving branch tip -- bump it deliberately so a build can be reproduced and
# its pins re-checked. Snapshots get their own tag family
# (cu<cuda>-sm120-main...) and never move :latest.
# These VLLM_MAIN_* values are used by VLLM_REF=main ONLY. Any other ref takes
# the DEFAULT_* set, so a hand-run VLLM_REF=<sha> must bring its own
# FLASHINFER_REF *and* TORCH_REF / TORCHVISION_VERSION when the target wants
# something other than the release pins; ./container/preflight refuses the
# mismatch loudly instead of building it quietly.
# main @ 2026-10-15 (was 698e79f, 2026-10-13): torch 2.14.0 / flashinfer 0.7.1.
VLLM_MAIN_SHA=4d9a8d6a417afad932b368471e498ca75a03b942
VLLM_MAIN_FLASHINFER_REF=v0.7.1
# vLLM main took torch 2.14.0 / torchvision 0.29.0 in vllm#52183 (2026-10-14,
# commit 27 of the 165 in the 698e79f..4d9a8d6 range). The release set stays on
# 2.13.0 / 0.28.0, so the snapshot overrides its own instead of dragging v0.29.0
# -- and every other launcher's image -- onto a torch it was never tested with.
# This is the first repin to move torch; the divergence is an owner decision, not
# a default, and it is why a snapshot bump is no longer a one-variable edit.
# torchaudio is deliberately absent: main still pins 2.11.0 *next to* torch
# 2.14.0, so that is upstream's own pairing, and a second knob asserting one value
# only invites drift. It is also the one source-built stage whose ABI partner
# moved -- torchaudio-build is FROM torch-build, so v2.11.0 now compiles against
# 2.14 headers. The CUDA-minor import check is unaffected (both sides 13.2);
# whether v2.11.0's sources compile is NOT VERIFIED until that stage runs.
VLLM_MAIN_TORCH_REF=v2.14.0
VLLM_MAIN_TORCHVISION_VERSION=0.29.0
# The release a snapshot of main is heading for. Cosmetic: it only prefixes the
# .dev version and nothing compares it. Bump when a new vX.Y.0 is cut.
# 0.33.0 since 2026-10-13: v0.32.0 sits on a release branch cut from main at
# fe341a53dd (2026-10-12; rc0 tagged), and the snapshots are past that point, so
# a 0.32.0.dev version would sort *below* a release it is ahead of. The bump was
# already due at the previous pin: df6c7ad is 13 commits past that same cut, so
# this catches the prefix up rather than reacting to 698e79f. (Same move as
# 0.31.0 -> 0.32.0 on 2026-10-01, after the 3d5f4d4cd5 cut.)
# Still 0.33.0 at 4d9a8d6 (2026-10-15): v0.32.0 is still the newest release
# branch and its cut point is still fe341a53dd, so a 165-commit jump crossed no
# new cut. v0.32.0rc1/rc2 were tagged inside this window; rc's are not cuts.
DEFAULT_VLLM_NEXT_VERSION=0.33.0
